From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:40:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: add cooling, CAMSS/CCI and GPU
 fixes

Adds SoC-level devicetree content the Google Pixel 2 XL (taimen) port
needs, applicable to any msm8998 board:

- #cooling-cells on cpu0-7 and adreno_gpu, plus cooling-maps for each
  CPU and GPU thermal zone. msm8998.dtsi previously had no thermal
  throttling wired up at all.

- adreno_gpu opp-microvolt corrections, taken from downstream's GFX
  CPR4 open-loop ceilings, so the 670 MHz and 515 MHz OPPs are no
  longer under-volted relative to their voltage rail's ceiling.

- adreno_smmu: drop "qcom,adreno-smmu" from the compatible string.
  That opts the Adreno A540 into split-TTBR per-process pagetables,
  and CP_SMMU_TABLE_UPDATE context switching faults on this part
  (49-bit-truncated global VAs in the FAR), wedging the GPU on app
  launches and eventually the whole SoC via a stuck
  gcc_gpu_bimc_gfx_clk. Plain pagetables keep every engine in low
  TTBR0 space.

- CAMSS and CCI device nodes, disabled by default and enabled per
  board. camss.c has no msm8998 match yet; msm8998 and sdm660 CAMSS
  are the same IP at the same addresses bar the CSIPHY register base,
  so the node is deliberately inert until the driver half lands, and
  binds to nothing in the meantime.

- cci0/cci1 and cam_mclk0/1 pinctrl states, and the mmss watchdog
  node (this SoC's only unconditional way back from a boot that never
  completes -- the bootloader does not leave it armed for Linux).

CAMSS carries no interconnects/interconnect-names property: unlike
this port's 6.0 base, 6.18's msm8998.dtsi has no interconnect
provider nodes (no bimc/mnoc) at all, so &mnoc/&bimc do not resolve.
Bandwidth voting can be added back once an interconnect provider
lands in this dtsi.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
